# Project Context (PRD)

CRITICAL: You MUST read the file `docs/PRD.md` at the start of every conversation (before taking any action). This is the Product Requirements Document and the single source of truth for what needs to be built.

The PRD includes:
- Product summary, context, and problem statement
- General and specific objectives, and success metrics (KPIs)
- Scope (in scope / out of scope / by phase)
- Functional requirements (RF-###) and non-functional requirements
- Business rules, high-level data model, architecture and stack
- Integrations, design/UX references, constraints, risks, roadmap, and open questions

Do not proceed with any task until you have read and understood `docs/PRD.md`.
